.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on runs cancel command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for run cancellation; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for run cancellation; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for run cancellation; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON run
cancellation result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the run cancellation prompt and human
result; --yes is still required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs cancel run_123
Canceled run_123
.sp
# Standard error:
Cancel run run_123? [y/N]
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Without --yes, table mode prompts only when stdin is a
#        terminal. Redirected, JSON, and quiet execution require --yes.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs cancel run_123 --yes
Canceled run_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS get
.EX
axilio runs get <run-id>
.EE

.PP
Fetch one run by the ID returned from \fBruns list\fR or \fBruns start\fR\&.

.PP
The result includes status, trigger, workflow, session, phone, created,
started and completed times, error message, and video URL when present.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the run-detail request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the run-detail request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
run-detail result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the run-detail request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the run-detail result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the run-detail
request; the run-detail result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs get run_123
Run        run_123
Status     completed
Trigger    manual
Workflow   <workflow-id>
Session    <session-id>
Phone      <phone-id>
Created    <created-at>
Started    <started-at>
Completed  <completed-at>
Error      -
Video      <video-url>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs get run_123 -o json
{
  "id": "run_123",
  "status": "completed",
  "trigger": "manual",
  "workflow_id": "<workflow-id>",
  "session_id": "<session-id>",
  "phone_id": "<phone-id>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Shortened representative JSON output; timestamps, errors, and
#        video URL appear when available.
.EE

.SS history
.EX
axilio runs history [flags]
.EE

.PP
List the caller's historic runs between --from and --to, including
archived runs that \fBruns list\fR no longer returns. Filter by workflow,
final status (repeatable), or a run/workflow ID substring with --search.

.PP
Page with --limit and --offset. Accepts an RFC 3339 timestamp
(2026-08-01T00:00:00Z) or a bare YYYY-MM-DD date, which reads as
midnight UTC of that day.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--from\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Start of the query window (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum runs in this page (1-500) (default
"50")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--offset\fP=\fInumber\fP - Number of matching runs to skip before this
page
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--search\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Filter by run or workflow ID substring
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--status\fP=\fIstringSlice\fP - Restrict to run statuses: queued,
running, completed, failed, cancelled (repeatable) (default "[]")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--to\fP=\fIvalue\fP - End of the query window (default: now)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--workflow\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Return only runs for this workflow ID

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the run-history request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the run-history request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
run-history result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the run-history request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the run-history result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the run-history
request; the run-history result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs history --from 2026-08-01
RUN ID   STATUS     TRIGGER  WORKFLOW      STARTED      COMPLETED
<run-id> completed  manual   <workflow-id> <timestamp>  <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: --from is required; an omitted --to means now. Bare dates read
#        as midnight UTC. An empty successful result prints No runs
#        found.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs history --from 2026-08-01 --to 2026-08-22 --workflow wf_123 --status failed
RUN ID   STATUS  TRIGGER  WORKFLOW  STARTED      COMPLETED
<run-id> failed  manual   wf_123    <timestamp>  <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs history
.sp
# Standard error:
--from is required. Accepts an RFC 3339 timestamp (2026-08-01T00:00:00Z) or a bare YYYY-MM-DD date, which reads as midnight UTC of that day.
.sp
# Exit status: 2
# Notes: The window is validated before credentials or an API request.
.EE

.SS start
.EX
axilio runs start <workflow-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Create runs for a workflow ID discovered with \fBworkflows list\fR\&.

.PP
--count creates that many run configurations and must be between 1 and
1000, inclusive.

.PP
--phone-id pins every created run to a specific dedicated phone.

.PP
--variables is a JSON object of run variables, exposed to workflow code
as the \fBvariables\fR dict; every created run receives the same object.
Values are stored and delivered in plaintext - do not put secrets here.

.PP
--start-timeout is the number of whole seconds a queued run may wait for
a phone before auto-cancel, between 60 and 86400 inclusive; zero or
negative values omit the field and use the server default (300).

.PP
--watch follows the single created run to completion exactly like \fBruns
watch\fR, and requires --count 1.

.PP
Successful output contains the created run IDs.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--count\fP=\fInumber\fP - Number of run configurations to create (1-1000)
(default "1")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-id\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Dedicated phone ID to pin to every created
run
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--start-timeout\fP=\fInumber\fP - Queued-phone wait in whole seconds,
60-86400, such as 300 or 900; 0 or negative values use the server
default
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--variables\fP=\fIvalue\fP - JSON object of run variables applied to
every created run (plaintext; no secrets)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--watch\fP - Follow the created run to completion (requires --count
1)

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on runs start command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the run-create request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the run-create request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the run-create request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit created run IDs as human messages
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress table-mode run IDs and guidance; a JSON
result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123
Started run <run-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: -o json emits the complete run_ids response on stdout. --count
#        accepts 1 through 1000, inclusive.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123 --count 3
Started run <run-id-1>
Started run <run-id-2>
Started run <run-id-3>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123 --count 0
.sp
# Standard error:
--count must be between 1 and 1000 (got 0)
.sp
# Exit status: 2
# Notes: The range is validated before credentials, allocation, or an
#        API request.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123 --phone-id ph_123
Started run <run-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 5\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123 --start-timeout 300
Started run <run-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 6\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123 --watch
Started run <run-id>
<frame stream>
✓ Run <run-id> completed
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Run <run-id> queued — waiting for a phone
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Follows the created run exactly like `runs watch`; requires
#        --count 1.
.EE

.SS stats
.EX
axilio runs stats <workflow-id>
.EE

.PP
Report how a workflow has performed for the caller: total runs across
all states, plus the success rate among runs that finished (completed or
failed - queued, running, and canceled runs are not in the rate's
denominator).

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the run-stats request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the run-stats request; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
run-stats result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the run-stats request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the run-stats result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the run-stats request;
the run-stats result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs stats wf_123
Workflow      wf_123
Total runs    8
Success rate  87.5% of finished runs
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The rate's denominator is completed plus failed runs; total
#        runs counts every state.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs stats wf_123 -o json
{
  "total_runs": 8,
  "success_rate": 0.875
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS watch
.EX
axilio runs watch <run-id>
.EE

.PP
Follow a run live: wait for it to start, then stream its session's
telemetry (output logs and completed spans) until the session ends, and
exit with the run's outcome. Watching an already-finished run replays
its recorded telemetry and exits the same way.

.PP
The exit code reflects the outcome: 0 when the run completed, 1 when it
failed (the error message is printed), 7 when it was canceled or the
watch was interrupted. Interrupting the watch does not affect the run;
re-run \fBruns watch\fR to replay and resume following.

.PP
JSON mode streams newline-delimited JSON rather than a single document:
one object per telemetry frame in archive order, then a final
\fB{"watch_end": true, ...}\fR object carrying the run's status and error
message.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the run polling and frame reads;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the run polling and frame reads;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
telemetry stream
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the run polling and frame reads;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Stream frames as human lines or
newline-delimited JSON (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr progress notes; the frame stream
remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs watch run_123
<time>  span  sdk_call    Screen.observe  250ms
<time>  INFO  output_log  <workflow output>
✓ Run run_123 completed
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Run run_123 running — streaming session <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Streams the session's telemetry — logs and completed spans —
#        until the session ends. Exit 0 on completed, 1 on failed (with
#        the run's error message), 7 on canceled or interrupt. Watching
#        a finished run replays its telemetry.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs watch run_123 -o json
{"watch_end":true,"run_id":"run_123","status":"completed"}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: JSON mode is newline-delimited, not a single document: one
#        object per telemetry frame in archive order (unknown kinds pass
#        through verbatim), then the watch_end summary — carrying status
#        and error_message — as the final line.
.EE

.SH sessions
.EX
axilio sessions
.EE

.PP
Manage the phone sessions used by \fBaxilio phone\fR\&. Sessions remain active
in Axilio until stopped; the CLI saves connection information locally so
later phone commands can reconnect. Session selection precedence is
--session, AXILIO_SESSION, the only locally saved session, the most
recently started session, then an ambiguity error. \fBsessions list
--remote\fR asks the API for all active Axilio sessions, including
sessions not saved on this computer.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio sessions\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
sessions --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not acquire, list,
select, or stop sessions. Global flags shown here therefore have no
effect. Pass flags to a sessions subcommand instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on sessions command; bare
axilio sessions only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio sessions list
axilio sessions start
axilio sessions current
axilio sessions get sess_123
axilio sessions trace sess_123
axilio sessions downloads sess_123
axilio sessions stop sess_123
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio sessions list [flags]
.EE

.PP
List sessions saved locally by default. The \fB*\fR marker identifies the
session that phone commands would select in this shell when selection is
not ambiguous. Use --remote to list all active Axilio sessions instead;
remote rows include session ID, phone ID, phone type, and model but do
not indicate which session this CLI would select.

.PP
Use --history for the org's full session history, active and released.
Any history filter flag switches to history mode on its own: status,
source, phone type, search, workflow, and started/ended time bounds,
plus sort, order, and offset. Time bounds accept RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD.
Inspect a returned ID with \fBsessions get\fR or \fBsessions trace\fR\&.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--ended-after\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Only sessions released at or after this
time
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--ended-before\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Only sessions released at or before this
time
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--history\fP - List the org's session history, active and released
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum history rows to return (1-100) (default
"50")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--offset\fP=\fInumber\fP - History rows to skip for pagination
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--order\fP=\fIvalue\fP - History sort direction: asc|desc
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--remote\fP - List all active Axilio sessions instead of sessions
saved locally
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--search\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Case-insensitive match on phone, session, or
workflow
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--sort\fP=\fIvalue\fP - History sort column:
started|ended|status|duration|source
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--source\fP=\fIstringSlice\fP - Filter history by source:
workflow|interactive (repeatable) (default "[]")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--started-after\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Only sessions started at or after this
time
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--started-before\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Only sessions started at or before this
time
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--status\fP=\fIstringSlice\fP - Filter history by status:
active|completed|cancelled|expired (repeatable) (default "[]")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--type\fP=\fIstringSlice\fP - Filter history by phone type:
shared|dedicated (repeatable) (default "[]")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--workflow\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Only sessions for this workflow ID

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Authenticates only --remote listing; no effect
on sessions saved locally
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Selects the API host only with --remote; no
effect on sessions saved locally
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable session
listing
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Selects the OAuth org only with --remote; no
effect on sessions saved locally
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render local or remote sessions as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes; the session listing
remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions list
SESSION       PHONE       TYPE
*  <session-id>  <phone-id>  android
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: With no sessions saved locally, stdout explains how to start
#        one and exit status is 0.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions list --remote
SESSION       PHONE       TYPE     MODEL
<session-id>  <phone-id>  android  Pixel 8
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Remote results come from the API and do not mark the session
#        selected by this CLI.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions list -o json
[
  {
    "session_id": "<session-id>",
    "phone_id": "<phone-id>",
    "phone_type": "android",
    "control_url": "<control-url>",
    "created_at": "<timestamp>"
  }
]
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Locally saved session JSON includes the stored control URL; IDs
#        and URLs vary.
.EE

.SS current
.EX
axilio sessions current
.EE

.PP
Resolve and show the session selected for phone commands.

.PP
Phone command session selection precedence is --session, AXILIO_SESSION,
the only locally saved session, the most recently started session, then
an ambiguity error. This command has no --session flag, so it starts at
AXILIO_SESSION. If no session can be selected, the command exits with
not-found status 4.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect on sessions
current command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
current-session result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the current-session result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for session resolution;
the current-session result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions current
Session  <session-id>
Phone    <phone-id>
Type     android
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: When no session can be selected, all output modes leave stdout
#        empty and exit with not-found status 4.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % AXILIO_SESSION=sess_123 axilio sessions current
Session  sess_123
Phone    <phone-id>
Type     android
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The named session must be saved locally; AXILIO_SESSION takes
#        precedence over automatic session selection.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions current -o json
{
  "session_id": "<session-id>",
  "phone_id": "<phone-id>",
  "phone_type": "android",
  "control_url": "<control-url>",
  "created_at": "<timestamp>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: A selected session keeps the same JSON shape. With no selected
#        session, stdout is empty and exit status is 4.
.EE

.SS downloads
.EX
axilio sessions downloads <session-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
List one session's captured downloads, newest first — the direct answer
to "what did this session download".

.PP
Rows appear at detection, before the bytes finish moving, so a caller
waiting on a file watches its capture state progress rather than an
empty list. Save a ready capture with \fBdownloads get\fR\&. Filters and
paging match \fBdownloads list\fR\&.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--created-after\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Only captures registered at or after
this RFC 3339 time
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--created-before\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Only captures registered at or before
this RFC 3339 time
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum captures in this page (1-100) (default
"50")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--max-size\fP=\fInumber\fP - Only captures at most this many bytes; 0
means no bound
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--mime\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Only captures of exactly this media type, e.g.
image/png
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--min-size\fP=\fInumber\fP - Only captures at least this many bytes; 0
means no bound
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--offset\fP=\fInumber\fP - Number of matching captures to skip before
this page
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--search\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Filter filenames by case-insensitive substring

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the session-download request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the session-download request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
session-download result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the session-download request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the session-download result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the session-download
request; the session-download result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions downloads sess_123
ID       FILENAME     SIZE     TYPE       STATE  SESSION  CREATED
<dl-id>  receipt.png  2.0 KiB  image/png  ready  sess_123 <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Rows appear at detection, before the bytes finish moving; watch
#        STATE progress to ready, then save with `downloads get`.
.EE

.SS get
.EX
axilio sessions get <session-id>
.EE

.PP
Fetch one session by ID, active or historical.

.PP
The result includes status, source, phone, allocation and release times,
duration, tags, workflow, capture and telemetry settings, and the
recording status and playback URL when ready. Active sessions also
include a short-lived screen thumbnail URL. Discover IDs with \fBsessions
list --remote\fR or \fBsessions list --history\fR\&.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the session-detail request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the session-detail request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
session-detail result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the session-detail request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the session-detail result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the session-detail
request; the session-detail result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions get sess_123
Session        sess_123
Name           -
Status         completed
Source         workflow
Allocated by   api_run
Phone          <phone-id>
Phone name     -
Nickname       -
Model          Pixel 8
Type           android
Location       us-central
Dedicated      false
Workflow       <workflow-id>
Workflow name  demo
Allocated      2026-08-05 20:00
Released       2026-08-05 20:12
Duration       12m00s
Tags           team=qa
Capture        true
Telemetry      true
Recording      ready
Recording URL  <recording-url>
Thumbnail URL  -
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Works for active and released sessions; the thumbnail URL is
#        present on active sessions only.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions get sess_123 -o json
{
  "session_id": "sess_123",
  "status": "active",
  "source": "interactive",
  "phone_id": "<phone-id>",
  "allocated_at": "<timestamp>",
  "recording_status": "pending",
  "thumbnail_status": "ready",
  "thumbnail_url": "<thumbnail-url>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Excerpt: JSON is the canonical session detail response plus
#        thumbnail_status/thumbnail_url enrichment on active sessions.
.EE

.SS start
.EX
axilio sessions start [flags]
.EE

.PP
Acquire an Android phone.

.PP
The CLI currently supports Android allocation only; --phone-type remains
available for scripts that pass android explicitly, and any other value
is a usage error. The session remains active in Axilio until stopped;
the CLI saves its connection information locally and marks it as the
most recently started session. Pin a dedicated phone discovered through
\fBphones mine\fR with --phone-id, or attach the session to a workflow with
--workflow. --export prints only \fBexport AXILIO_SESSION=\\<id\\>\fR for
shell eval and cannot be combined with -o json.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--export\fP - Print only \fBexport AXILIO_SESSION=\\<id\\>\fR for shell
eval
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-id\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Pin a dedicated phone ID from \fBphones mine\fR
instead of pool allocation
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-type\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Phone platform to allocate (currently only
android) (default "android")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--workflow\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Workflow ID to attach; omit for an
interactive session

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
allocated-session result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the allocated session as table
or json; --export emits shell text and rejects json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress session guidance; the result or
--export text remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start
Session      <session-id>
Phone        <phone-id>
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.sp
# Standard error:
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start --phone-id ph_123
Session      <session-id>
Phone        ph_123
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.sp
# Standard error:
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start --workflow wf_123
Session      <session-id>
Phone        <phone-id>
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.sp
# Standard error:
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start --export
export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: --export is exact shell text; combining it with -o json is a
#        usage error before allocation.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 5\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % eval "$(axilio sessions start --export)"
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The shell consumes the nested command's export line and sets
#        AXILIO_SESSION in the current shell.
.EE

.SS stop
.EX
axilio sessions stop <session-id|phone-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Release an active phone allocation using either its session ID or phone
ID.

.PP
Discover IDs with \fBsessions list --remote\fR; matching locally saved
session information and the most-recent-session marker are removed after
release. JSON output is the canonical API deallocation response,
including the phone, session, workflow, and deallocation time. Without
--yes, table mode prompts only when stdin is a terminal. Redirected,
JSON, and quiet execution do not prompt and require --yes.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP - Release without prompting; required in JSON,
quiet, or redirected execution

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on sessions stop command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for session release; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for session release; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for session release; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
session release result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the session release prompt and human
result; --yes is still required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions stop sess_123
Released <phone-id>.
.sp
# Standard error:
Release <phone-id>? [y/N]
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Without --yes, table mode prompts only when stdin is a
#        terminal. Redirected, JSON, and quiet execution require --yes.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions stop ph_123 --yes
Released ph_123.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions stop ph_123 --yes -o json
{
  "deallocated_at": "<timestamp>",
  "phone_id": "ph_123",
  "session_id": "<session-id>",
  "workflow_id": "<workflow-id>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: JSON is the canonical API deallocation response; workflow_id
#        may be empty for an interactive session.
.EE

.SS trace
.EX
axilio sessions trace <session-id>
.EE

.PP
Fetch the durable telemetry frames for a session and render them as an
ordered listing of spans and logs with durations and billed costs.

.PP
Costs join at read time: sdk_call spans price by span ID and inference
spans by inference ID, in microdollars as billed. All pages are fetched,
so the output is the complete archived trace; frames with an
unrecognized kind are listed generically rather than dropped. JSON
output is the canonical frames response (frames, sdk_call_costs,
inference_costs, totals) merged across pages. A live --follow mode is
planned to arrive with the SDK's telemetry transport.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the telemetry-frames requests;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the telemetry-frames requests;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
trace result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the telemetry-frames requests;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the trace result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the telemetry-frames
requests; the trace result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions trace sess_123
TIME          KIND      NAME            DURATION  STATUS  COST
20:00:01.000  session   session         12m00s    ok      -
20:00:02.000  sdk_call  Screen.observe  1.0s      ok      $0.0031
20:00:02.100  inference inference       800ms     ok      $0.0020
20:00:03.500  log:output_log  hello     -         INFO    -
.sp
# Standard error:
1204 frames; billed sdk_call cost $0.0311
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Costs are billed microdollars: sdk_call spans price by span ID,
#        inference spans by inference ID. Frames with an unknown kind
#        are listed generically, never dropped.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions trace sess_123 -o json
{
  "frames": [
    {
      "kind": "span",
      "span_id": "<span-id>",
      "span_type": "sdk_call",
      "name": "Screen.observe",
      "start_time_unix_nano": 0,
      "end_time_unix_nano": 0
    }
  ],
  "sdk_call_costs": {"<span-id>": 3100},
  "inference_costs": {"<inference-id>": 2000},
  "total": 1204,
  "retention_expired": false
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Excerpt: the canonical frames response merged across all pages,
#        so the document is the complete archived trace.
.EE

.SH status
.EX
axilio status
.EE

.PP
Make an authenticated API request and report status, effective API host,
active organization selector, and account balance.

.PP
A valid API key or OAuth session is required. Use -o json for the
structured status, api_host, active_org, and balance fields.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the status request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the status request; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
status result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the status request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the status result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the status request;
the status result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio status
Status      ok
API host    https://api.axilio.ai/api/v1
Active org  (session default)
Balance     $5.00
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio status -o json
{
  "active_org": "",
  "api_host": "https://api.axilio.ai/api/v1",
  "balance": "$5.00",
  "status": "ok"
