.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Balance and active organization vary by account.
.EE

.SH upgrade
.EX
axilio upgrade [flags]
.EE

.PP
Download the latest release from GitHub and replace this binary in place
(the download is checksum-verified).

.PP
Homebrew installs defer to \fBbrew upgrade\fR, and development or \fBgo
install\fR builds are left to the Go toolchain. On a release build,
--check reports whether a newer release exists without installing it,
including for Homebrew-managed installations.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--check\fP - Check for a newer release without installing it

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on upgrade command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit human upgrade guidance or a JSON
upgrade-status result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress human upgrade guidance and status; JSON
still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio upgrade --check
A newer release is available: <old> -> <new>. Run `axilio upgrade` to install.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The version placeholders vary. Homebrew installations perform
#        the same release check but name `brew upgrade axilio` as the
#        next command. Up-to-date, no-release, and development builds
#        report their own state.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio upgrade
Upgraded to <latest-version>.
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Upgrading axilio <current-version> -> <latest-version>...
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Standalone release only; development builds and
#        Homebrew-managed installs print their own package-manager
#        guidance.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % brew upgrade axilio
.sp
# External behavior: Output and exit status are owned by Homebrew, not
#                    the axilio CLI.
.EE

.SH uploads
.EX
axilio uploads
.EE

.PP
Manage the org file library. Files live here until deleted and can be
pushed to any phone the org holds, so one upload serves many phones.
\fBadd\fR stores a local file, \fBlist\fR discovers uploads and quota, \fBpush\fR
delivers a stored upload, and \fBdelete\fR frees library quota. \fBphone send\fR
combines add and push for the selected session's phone.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio uploads\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
uploads --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not add, list,
push, or delete uploads. Global flags shown here therefore have no
effect. Pass flags to an uploads subcommand instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on uploads command; bare
axilio uploads only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio uploads list
axilio uploads add ./photo.jpg
axilio uploads push upl_123 --phone-id ph_123
axilio uploads delete upl_123 --yes
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio uploads list [flags]
.EE

.PP
List uploads and standing storage quota for the active organization.

.PP
Results include upload ID, filename, size, MIME type, status, and
creation time. Page with --limit and --offset, search filenames by
case-insensitive substring, and sort by created_at, filename, or
size_bytes in asc or desc order. Omitting sort/order uses server
defaults.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum files in this page (1-100) (default
"50")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--offset\fP=\fInumber\fP - Number of matching files to skip before this
page
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--order\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Sort direction: asc or desc; omitted uses server
default
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--search\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Filter filenames by case-insensitive substring
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--sort\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Sort key: created_at, filename, or size_bytes;
omitted uses server default

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the upload-list request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the upload-list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
upload-list result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the upload-list request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the upload-list result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the upload-list
request; the upload-list result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads list
ID          FILENAME   SIZE     TYPE        STATUS  CREATED
<upload-id> photo.jpg  2.0 MiB  image/jpeg  ready   <timestamp>
.sp
# Standard error:
1 of 10000 files, 2.0 MiB of 50.0 GiB used
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: An empty page still reports quota usage; the current global
#        limits are 10000 files and 50 GiB.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads list --search receipt --limit 20 --offset 0
ID          FILENAME     SIZE      TYPE       STATUS  CREATED
<upload-id> receipt.jpg  512.0 KiB image/jpeg ready   <timestamp>
.sp
# Standard error:
1 of 10000 files, 512.0 KiB of 50.0 GiB used
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Results and bytes used vary by organization; the limits are
#        global.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads list --sort filename --order asc
ID          FILENAME   SIZE     TYPE        STATUS  CREATED
<upload-id> photo.jpg  2.0 MiB  image/jpeg  ready   <timestamp>
.sp
# Standard error:
1 of 10000 files, 2.0 MiB of 50.0 GiB used
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Rows are sorted by filename ascending; results and bytes used
#        vary by organization.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads list -o json
{
  "files": [
    {
      "id": "<upload-id>",
      "filename": "photo.jpg",
      "size_bytes": 2097152,
      "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
      "status": "ready",
      "created_at": "<timestamp>"
    }
  ],
  "total": 1,
  "usage": {
    "file_count": 1,
    "file_limit": 10000,
    "total_bytes": 2097152,
    "byte_limit": 53687091200
  }
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Representative response; files, result count, and bytes used
#        vary by organization; limits are global.
.EE

.SS add
.EX
axilio uploads add <path> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Register a local file, upload its bytes, and verify them, leaving a
ready file in the library.

.PP
Use \fBaxilio uploads push\fR to send it to a phone, or \fBaxilio phone send\fR
to do both in one step. The stored filename defaults to the local
basename and MIME type is inferred from the extension; --filename and
--mime-type override those values. The library stores files up to 1 GiB,
including files too large to deliver to a phone (phone delivery is
limited to 100 MiB per file).

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--filename\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Stored filename; omitted uses the local
file's basename
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--mime-type\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Stored MIME type; omitted infers it from the
file extension

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the file-upload request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the file-upload request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
stored-upload result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the file-upload request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the stored-upload result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress upload progress; the stored-upload
result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads add ./photo.jpg
ID        <upload-id>
Filename  photo.jpg
Size      2.0 MiB
Type      image/jpeg
Status    ready
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Uploading photo.jpg
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads add ./asset --filename photo.jpg --mime-type image/jpeg
ID        <upload-id>
Filename  photo.jpg
Size      2.0 MiB
Type      image/jpeg
Status    ready
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Uploading asset
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: --filename and --mime-type override values inferred from the
#        local path.
.EE

.SS delete
.EX
axilio uploads delete <upload-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Delete an upload from the active organization's library and free its
storage quota.

.PP
Use \fBuploads list\fR to discover the upload ID. Deletion also schedules
removal from every phone holding or receiving a copy. Without --yes,
table mode prompts only when stdin is a terminal. Redirected, JSON, and
quiet execution do not prompt and require --yes. The alias \fBuploads rm\fR
performs the same operation.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP - Delete without prompting; required in JSON, quiet,
or redirected execution

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on uploads delete command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the upload-delete request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the upload-delete request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the upload-delete request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
deletion result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the prompt and human confirmation;
--yes is required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads delete upl_123
Deleted upl_123
.sp
# Standard error:
Delete upload upl_123? Also recall it from phones holding or receiving a copy? [y/N]
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Table mode prompts only when stdin is a terminal. Redirected,
#        JSON, and quiet execution require --yes.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads rm upl_123 --yes
Deleted upl_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS push
.EX
axilio uploads push <upload-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Send a stored library file to a phone's media library.

.PP
Unlike \fBaxilio phone send\fR this uploads nothing, so the same file can be
pushed to many phones without re-uploading it or consuming more quota.
--phone-id is required and can be discovered with \fBphones mine\fR or
\fBsessions list --remote\fR\&. The collection is inferred unless DCIM,
Pictures, or Movies is selected. Phone delivery is limited to 100 MiB
per file; the server rejects a stored file above that even though the
library holds it. By default the command returns after dispatch; --wait
blocks for delivered or failed, and --timeout applies only with --wait.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--collection\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Target DCIM, Pictures, or Movies; omitted
infers from media type
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-id\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Target phone ID from \fBphones mine\fR or remote
sessions (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--timeout\fP=\fIduration\fP - Maximum delivery wait, such as 30s, 1m30s,
or 2m; applies only with --wait (default 1m). Units: ns, us/µs, ms, s,
m, h.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--wait\fP - Block until the phone reports delivered or failed instead
of returning at dispatch

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the file-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the file-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
delivery result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the file-delivery request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the delivery result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress delivery progress and notes; the
delivery result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads push upl_123 --phone-id ph_123
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    dispatched
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Pushing upl_123 to phone ph_123
pushed without requesting delivery receipt. In the future, add --wait if you want the cli to wait for delivery confirmation and report result.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads push upl_123 --phone-id ph_123 --collection Pictures
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    dispatched
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Pushing upl_123 to phone ph_123
pushed without requesting delivery receipt. In the future, add --wait if you want the cli to wait for delivery confirmation and report result.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The phone receives the file in Pictures.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads push upl_123 --phone-id ph_123 --wait --timeout 2m
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    delivered
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Pushing upl_123 to phone ph_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: With --wait, the command returns only after delivered, failed,
#        or the two-minute deadline.
.EE

.SH usage
.EX
axilio usage
.EE

.PP
Read the active organization's usage: aggregate spend and compute
metrics over a reporting window, or the individual billed inference
calls behind the inference line item.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio usage\fR without a subcommand only displays this help.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on usage command; bare axilio
usage only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio usage metrics --from 2026-08-01
axilio usage inferences --from 2026-08-01 --endpoint locate
.EE

.SS inferences
.EX
axilio usage inferences [flags]
.EE

.PP
List the billed vision inference calls between --from and --to, most
recent first, with the cost and latency of each. Filter by endpoint
(detect or locate, repeatable), model, or session; --search matches
inference-ID substrings.

.PP
--order-by is a '<field> <asc|desc>\&' expression; the field is one of
created_at, cost_microdollars, latency_ms, endpoint, model, or
inference_id.

.PP
Page with --limit and --offset.

.PP
Accepts an RFC 3339 timestamp (2026-08-01T00:00:00Z) or a bare
YYYY-MM-DD date, which reads as midnight UTC of that day.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--endpoint\fP=\fIstringSlice\fP - Restrict to a vision endpoint: detect
or locate (repeatable) (default "[]")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--from\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Start of the query window (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum inference calls in this page (1-100)
(default "50")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--model\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Restrict to a single model name
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--offset\fP=\fInumber\fP - Number of matching calls to skip before this
page
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--order-by\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Sort expression '<field> <asc|desc>\&'
(default: created_at desc)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--search\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Filter by inference-ID substring
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Restrict to inferences that ran under one
phone session
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--to\fP=\fIvalue\fP - End of the query window (default: now)

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the inference-list request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the inference-list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
inference-list result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the inference-list request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the inference-list result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the inference-list
request; the inference-list result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio usage inferences --from 2026-08-01
TIME        INFERENCE ID   ENDPOINT  MODEL            COST     LATENCY  SESSION
<timestamp> <inference-id> locate    axilio-ground-1  $0.0012  321 ms   -
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Costs render in dollars from the API's microdollar amounts. An
#        empty successful result prints No inferences found.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio usage inferences --from 2026-08-01 --endpoint locate --session ses_123
TIME        INFERENCE ID   ENDPOINT  MODEL            COST     LATENCY  SESSION
<timestamp> <inference-id> locate    axilio-ground-1  $0.0012  321 ms   ses_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS metrics
.EX
axilio usage metrics [flags]
.EE

.PP
Summarize the organization's usage between --from and --to: total
compute minutes, spend split by product (sessions, inference, other),
and infrastructure costs, each with the change from the previous period.

.PP
--granularity picks the bucket resolution (hourly or daily); the server
chooses when omitted. --tz names an IANA timezone (e.g.
America/Los_Angeles) for bucketing periods.

.PP
Table mode prints the summary numbers; the per-period chart series are
available in --output json.

.PP
Accepts an RFC 3339 timestamp (2026-08-01T00:00:00Z) or a bare
YYYY-MM-DD date, which reads as midnight UTC of that day.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--from\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Start of the reporting window (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--granularity\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Bucket resolution: hourly or daily
(default: server-chosen)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--to\fP=\fIvalue\fP - End of the reporting window (default: now)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--tz\fP=\fIvalue\fP - IANA timezone for bucketing periods, such as
America/Los_Angeles

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the usage-metrics request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the usage-metrics request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
usage summary
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the usage-metrics request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the usage summary as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the usage-metrics
request; the usage summary remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio usage metrics --from 2026-08-01
Period           <start> - <end> (daily)
Compute minutes  42.5 (+10.0%)
Session spend    $1.25
Inference spend  $0.75
Other spend      $0.00
Infra cost       $2.00 total, $2.00 this period (-5.0%)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: --from is required; an omitted --to means now. Bare dates read
#        as midnight UTC. The per-period chart series are only in -o
#        json.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio usage metrics --from 2026-08-01 --to 2026-08-22 --granularity daily
Period           <start> - <end> (daily)
Compute minutes  42.5 (+10.0%)
Session spend    $1.25
Inference spend  $0.75
Other spend      $0.00
Infra cost       $2.00 total, $2.00 this period (-5.0%)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SH workflows
.EX
axilio workflows
.EE

.PP
Manage workflows in the active organization. \fBworkflows list\fR discovers
workflow IDs; create, get, and delete manage the records; pull, push,
revisions, and restore round-trip the Python source: pull the current
code to a file, edit locally, push it back as a new revision, and
restore any earlier revision. A workflow ID can be passed to \fBruns
start\fR or \fBsessions start --workflow\fR\&.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio workflows\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
workflows --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not list
workflows. Global flags shown here therefore have no effect. Pass flags
to a workflows subcommand instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on workflows command; bare
axilio workflows only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio workflows list
axilio workflows create checkout-flow --code checkout.py
axilio workflows pull wf_123 --out checkout.py
axilio workflows push wf_123 checkout.py -m "handle 2FA"
axilio runs start wf_123
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio workflows list [flags]
.EE

.PP
List workflows in the active organization, most recent first.

.PP
Results include workflow ID, name, platform, status, and last-run time.
Use --search for a name substring and --limit to control the number
returned. A listed workflow ID can be passed directly to \fBruns start\fR\&.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum number of most-recent workflows to
return (1-500) (default "20")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--search\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Filter workflow names by substring

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the workflow-list request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the workflow-list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
workflow-list result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the workflow-list request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the workflow-list result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the workflow-list
request; the workflow-list result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows list
WORKFLOW ID   NAME      PLATFORM  STATUS  LAST RUN
<workflow-id> Checkout  android   active  <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: An empty successful result prints No workflows found.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows list --search checkout --limit 10
WORKFLOW ID   NAME      PLATFORM  STATUS  LAST RUN
<workflow-id> Checkout  android   active  <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Names, IDs, statuses, and timestamps vary by organization.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows list -o json
{
  "limit": 20,
  "offset": 0,
  "total": 1,
  "workflows": [
    {
      "workflow": {
        "id": "<workflow-id>",
        "name": "Checkout",
        "platform": "android",
        "status": "active"
      }
    }
  ]
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Shortened representative JSON output; workflow records may
#        include additional fields and statistics.
.EE

.SS create
.EX
axilio workflows create <name> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Create a workflow in the active organization.

.PP
The name must contain only letters, digits, hyphens, and underscores,
and be unique within the org. Pass --code with a Python file to save the
workflow's first code revision atomically with it; omit it to create an
empty workflow and \fBworkflows push\fR code later. Recording, telemetry,
and capture default to on server-side; each toggle flag is sent only
when set explicitly, so omitted toggles keep the server defaults.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--capture\fP - Capture media produced on the phone into the org
library; --capture=false disables it (default "true")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--code\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Python file saved as the workflow's first code
revision
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--platform\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Target platform: ios, android, or both;
omitted uses the server default
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--recording\fP - Record this workflow's runs; --recording=false
suppresses video and thumbnails (default "true")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--telemetry\fP - Persist telemetry spans for runs; --telemetry=false
skips the durable trace store (default "true")

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the workflow-create request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the workflow-create request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
created-workflow result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the workflow-create request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the created-workflow result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the workflow-create
request; the created-workflow result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows create checkout-flow --platform android --code checkout.py
Workflow     <workflow-id>
Revision     1
Revision ID  <revision-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: With --code, the file is saved atomically as revision 1.
#        Without it, only the workflow ID prints.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows create checkout-flow --recording=false
Workflow  <workflow-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows create "bad name"
.sp
# Standard error:
workflow name must contain only letters, digits, hyphens, and underscores (got "bad name")
.sp
# Exit status: 2
# Notes: The name rule is validated before credentials or an API
#        request.
.EE

.SS delete
.EX
axilio workflows delete <workflow-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Delete a workflow from the active organization, including its code
revisions.

.PP
Runs already recorded against it are not removed. Without --yes, table
mode prompts only when stdin is a terminal. Redirected, JSON, and quiet
execution do not prompt and require --yes. The alias \fBworkflows rm\fR
performs the same operation.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP - Delete without prompting; required in JSON, quiet,
or redirected execution

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the workflow-delete request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the workflow-delete request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
deletion result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the workflow-delete request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
deletion result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the prompt and human confirmation;
--yes is required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows delete wf_123 --yes
Deleted wf_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Deletes the workflow and its code revisions; recorded runs
#        remain.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows delete wf_123 < /dev/null
.sp
# Standard error:
aborted (pass --yes to delete non-interactively)
.sp
# Exit status: 2
# Notes: Redirected, JSON, and quiet execution never prompt; they
#        require --yes.
.EE

.SS get
.EX
axilio workflows get <workflow-id>
.EE

.PP
Show a single workflow: name, platform, status, OCR engine, the
recording/telemetry/capture toggles, timestamps, and run statistics.

.PP
Use \fBworkflows list\fR to discover the workflow ID, \fBworkflows pull\fR for
its code, and \fBworkflows revisions\fR for its code history.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the workflow-detail request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the workflow-detail request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
workflow-detail result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the workflow-detail request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the workflow-detail result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the workflow-detail
request; the workflow-detail result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows get wf_123
Workflow      wf_123
Name          Checkout
Platform      android
Status        active
OCR engine    free
Recording     true
Telemetry     true
Capture       true
Created       <timestamp>
Updated       <timestamp>
Last run      <timestamp>
Total runs    4
Success rate  75%
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows get wf_123 -o json
{
  "stats": {
    "success_rate": 0.75,
    "total_runs": 4
  },
  "workflow": {
    "id": "wf_123",
    "name": "Checkout",
    "platform": "android",
    "status": "active"
  }
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Shortened representative JSON output; the workflow record
#        includes the full field set.
.EE

.SS pull
.EX
axilio workflows pull <workflow-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Fetch the Python source of the workflow's current code revision.

.PP
By default the source prints to stdout so it can be piped; --out writes
it to a file instead, overwriting existing contents without
confirmation. A workflow with no revisions yet yields empty source at
revision 0. Edit the pulled file locally and \fBworkflows push\fR it back as
a new revision.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--out\fP=\fIvalue\fP - File to write the source to; omitted prints it to
stdout

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the workflow-code request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the workflow-code request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
pulled-code result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the workflow-code request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render pulled code as raw stdout text
or a json document; --out writes the file either way (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the --out acknowledgment; pulled source
or JSON remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows pull wf_123
<the current revision's Python source>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The raw source prints to stdout so it can be piped or
#        redirected.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows pull wf_123 --out checkout.py
Wrote checkout.py (revision 3, <bytes> bytes)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: A new file requests mode 0644, subject to the process umask.
#        Overwriting an existing file preserves its mode while replacing
#        its contents.
.EE

.SS push
.EX
axilio workflows push <workflow-id> <file> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Save a local Python file as a new code revision of the workflow, with an
optional commit-style --message.

.PP
The server deduplicates against the current revision by content hash:
pushing unchanged source is a no-op that creates no revision. Source is
capped at 256 KiB. Use \fBworkflows revisions\fR to inspect history and
\fBworkflows restore\fR to return to an earlier revision.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-m\fP, \fB--message\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Commit-style note stored with the
revision

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the code-save request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the code-save request; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
saved-revision result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the code-save request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the saved-revision result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the code-save request;
the saved-revision result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows push wf_123 checkout.py -m "handle 2FA"
Saved revision 4 (<revision-id>)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The server deduplicates by content hash; unchanged source
#        reports a no-op and creates no revision.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows push wf_123 checkout.py -o json
{
  "no_op": false,
  "revision": 4,
  "revision_id": "<revision-id>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS restore
.EX
axilio workflows restore <workflow-id> <revision-id>
.EE

.PP
Create a new code revision containing the source of the named earlier
revision.

.PP
Nothing is deleted and the action is not deduplicated, so the restore
itself is visible in \fBworkflows revisions\fR history. Use \fBworkflows
revisions\fR to discover revision IDs.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the revision-restore request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the revision-restore request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
restored-revision result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the revision-restore request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the restored-revision result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the revision-restore
request; the restored-revision result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows restore wf_123 <revision-id>
Restored <revision-id> as new revision 5 (<new-revision-id>)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Restore copies the old source into a new revision; nothing is
#        deleted and the action stays visible in history.
.EE

.SS revisions
.EX
axilio workflows revisions <workflow-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
List the workflow's code revision history in reverse-chronological
order: revision number, revision ID, author, size, save time, and the
optional message.

.PP
Page older history with --before, which returns revisions numbered
strictly below the given revision number. A listed revision ID can be
passed to \fBworkflows restore\fR\&.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--before\fP=\fInumber\fP - Return revisions numbered below this; 0 starts
from the newest
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum revisions to return (1-200) (default
"50")

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the revision-list request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the revision-list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
revision-list result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the revision-list request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the revision-list result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the revision-list
request; the revision-list result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows revisions wf_123
REV  REVISION ID    AUTHOR     SIZE   CREATED      MESSAGE
4    <revision-id>  <user-id>  1.2 KiB <timestamp> handle 2FA
3    <revision-id>  <user-id>  1.1 KiB <timestamp> -
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Newest first. When a full page returns, a note names the
#        --before cursor for older history.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows revisions wf_123 --limit 10 --before 3
REV  REVISION ID    AUTHOR     SIZE   CREATED      MESSAGE
2    <revision-id>  <user-id>  1.0 KiB <timestamp> -
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE


.SH ENVIRONMENT
\fBAXILIO_API_KEY\fP : API credential. Precedence: --api-key,
AXILIO_API_KEY, saved config key, then the saved OAuth session.

.PP
\fBAXILIO_BASE_URL\fP : API host. Precedence: --base-url, AXILIO_BASE_URL,
saved base-url, then https://api.axilio.ai.

.PP
\fBAXILIO_ORG\fP : OAuth organization slug or ID. Precedence: --org,
AXILIO_ORG, saved active organization, then the OAuth session default.
API keys remain scoped to the organization that created them.

.PP
\fBAXILIO_SESSION\fP : Selects a locally saved phone session. Precedence:
--session, AXILIO_SESSION, the only locally saved session, the most
recently started session, then an ambiguity error.

.PP
\fBAXILIO_DASHBOARD_URL\fP : Overrides the dashboard host used for browser
OAuth. It does not change the API host.

.PP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fP : Moves config, OAuth fallback, locally saved
session, and update-check state from $HOME/.config to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME.

.PP
\fBNO_COLOR\fP : Set to 1 to disable ANSI color in help shown on a
terminal; text decoration may remain. When help is redirected,
CLICOLOR_FORCE=1 takes precedence and can restore ANSI color.

.PP
\fBCLICOLOR\fP : Set to 1 to request ANSI color in help when output is a
terminal and TERM is not dumb.

.PP
\fBCLICOLOR_FORCE\fP : Set to 1 to force ANSI color when help is
redirected or TERM=dumb. For redirected help, it takes precedence over
NO_COLOR.

.PP
\fBTERM\fP : TERM=dumb disables ANSI color in help unless CLICOLOR_FORCE=1
is set.


.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0 (ok)\fP : Success.

.PP
\fB1 (error)\fP : The command failed for a reason that does not fit a more
specific category.

.PP
\fB2 (usage)\fP : Invalid command syntax, argument count, or value; or the
API rejected the request as invalid (HTTP 400 or 422).

.PP
\fB3 (auth)\fP : Missing or invalid credentials, unauthorized access, or
permission denied (HTTP 401 or 403).

.PP
\fB4 (not-found)\fP : A requested resource, phone allocation, or on-screen
element was not found (HTTP 404).

.PP
\fB5 (timeout)\fP : The operation exceeded its timeout or deadline (HTTP
408).

.PP
\fB6 (unavailable)\fP : The Axilio service or phone connection was
unavailable, the phone was offline, the request was rate-limited, or the
server failed (HTTP 429 or 5xx).

.PP
\fB7 (canceled)\fP : The operation was canceled by the user, shell, or
system.


.SH FILES
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/config.json\fP : Saved API
key, API host, and active organization. A new file requests mode 0600;
umask may make it more restrictive. Overwriting preserves its mode.

.PP
\fBOS keychain: service axilio-cli, account oauth-tokens\fP : Preferred
storage for browser-OAuth access and refresh tokens.

.PP
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/oauth.json\fP : OAuth-token
fallback when the OS keychain is unavailable. A new file requests mode
0600; umask may make it more restrictive. Overwriting preserves its
mode.
.TP
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/sessions/<session-id>\&.json\fP
One mode-0600 locally saved session record containing the session ID,
phone ID, type, control URL, and creation time. These local records let
phone commands reconnect; deleting one does not stop the corresponding
Axilio session.

.PP
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/current-session\fP : Stores
the ID of the most recently started locally saved session. A new file
requests mode 0600; umask may make it more restrictive. Overwriting
preserves its mode.

.PP
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/update-check.json\fP : Daily
release-check cache. Failures reading or writing it do not fail
commands.

.PP
\fB\&./screenshot.png\fP : Default output of \fBaxilio phone screenshot\fR;
--out selects another path and existing contents are overwritten.

.PP
\fB\&.claude/skills/axilio/SKILL.md\fP : Agent instructions written by
\fBaxilio init --agent claude\fR\&.

.PP
\fBAGENTS.md\fP : Shared file updated inside Axilio markers by \fBaxilio
init --agent codex\fR\&.

.PP
\fB\&.cursor/rules/axilio.mdc\fP : Agent instructions written by \fBaxilio
init --agent cursor\fR\&.


.SH NOTES
.SS Resolution precedence
Credentials resolve in this order: --api-key, AXILIO_API_KEY, the saved
config API key, then the saved OAuth session.

.PP
The organization resolves from --org, AXILIO_ORG, the saved active
organization, then the OAuth session default. Note that each API key is
scoped to the organization that created it and cannot switch
organizations with --org.

.PP
API host resolves from --base-url, AXILIO_BASE_URL, saved base-url, then
https://api.axilio.ai.

.PP
Phone command session selection precedence is --session, AXILIO_SESSION,
the only locally saved session, the most recently started session, then
an ambiguity error.

.SS Output behavior
Table output for human readability is the default. Primary results and
action acknowledgments use stdout. Every successful runnable application
command emits exactly one JSON document with -o json. Built-in help,
completion, and version remain text. Sessions start --export emits shell
text for eval and cannot be combined with -o json.

.PP
Notes, progress, and prompts use stderr and are suppressed in JSON or
quiet mode. Warnings and errors also use stderr, but remain visible in
every mode. Quiet preserves primary result data while suppressing action
acknowledgments and other optional human output. Destructive commands
prompt only when stdin is a terminal; JSON, quiet, and redirected
execution require --yes where offered. API-key, base-URL, and
organization flags affect API-backed commands; they do not select a
local phone session.

.SS Error presentation
Error examples show the message text without terminal formatting. Actual
error output may include an ERROR heading, spacing, and ANSI color.


.SH EXAMPLES
Observe and act on a selected phone session:

.EX
axilio sessions start --phone-type android
axilio phone observe
axilio phone tap --query "the search box"
axilio phone type "coffee shops"
axilio phone observe
.EE

.PP
Start independent sessions in separate shells:

.EX
eval "$(axilio sessions start --export)"
axilio phone screenshot --out screenshot.png
.EE

.PP
Run a workflow and request machine-readable output:

.EX
axilio workflows list -o json
axilio runs start <workflow-id> --count 2 -o json
.EE


